HYDROGEN SPECTRAL SERIES
→ 535.1 → Optics / Spectroscopy
- 535 Optics (Light)

FUNDAMENTALS
  Discrete energy levels of H atom:
    En = -13.6 / n²   eV     (n = 1, 2, 3, …)
    E1 = -13.6 eV            (ground state)
    E∞ =  0 eV               (ionization limit)

  Photon emitted when electron drops n2 → n1 (n2 > n1):
    ΔE = E_n2 - E_n1 = hc / λ
    1/λ = ν̃ = RH (1/n1² - 1/n2²)

VARIABLES
  n1, n2   : principal quantum numbers (integers)
  RH       : Rydberg constant ≈ 1.097376 × 10⁷ m⁻¹
  λ        : wavelength
  ν̃        : wavenumber (1/λ)
  En       : energy of level n

SERIES (grouped by landing level n1)
  Lyman     n1 = 1   ultraviolet     λ ≈ 10–121 nm
  Balmer    n1 = 2   visible         λ ≈ 364–656 nm
  Paschen   n1 = 3   infrared        λ ≈ 820 nm–1.88 µm
  Brackett  n1 = 4   infrared        λ ≈ 1.46–4.05 µm
  Pfund     n1 = 5   infrared        λ ≈ 2.28–7.46 µm

  As n2 → ∞ the lines of each series converge
  to the series limit (ionization from that n1).
